3. Not included; used at run time on the player's PC
----------------------------------------------------

    Windows' own d3d12.dll / dxgi.dll; AMD's driver and, optionally, the AMD HIP runtime (amdhip64_7.dll);
    the game's own AMD FidelityFX DLLs (renamed by the launcher, never modified or redistributed); the player's
    own file of the original upscaler (read by the converter on the player's PC, never redistributed); OptiScaler (its own
    project, GPL-3.0; the launcher downloads the WrongGPU edition from its own release page, it is not part of
    this repository or of WrongGPU's packages).


4. Not included; bundled into the Linux AppImage when it is built
------------------------------------------------------------------

4.1 libjpeg-turbo 2.1.2 (Ubuntu 22.04's libjpeg-turbo8): JPEG decoding in the Linux launcher
    Files:    none in this repository; build-appimage.sh installs libjpeg-turbo8-dev from the Ubuntu 22.04 archive and
              linuxdeploy copies libjpeg.so.8 into the AppImage, unmodified. The AppImage carries this file in
              share/doc/wronggpu/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.
    Source:   https://github.com/libjpeg-turbo/libjpeg-turbo, tag 2.1.2 (the source of Ubuntu's package)
    Licence:  the IJG (Independent JPEG Group) licence for the libjpeg API library, which the launcher uses, and the
